{
  "id": null,
  "uid": "epn8n-queue",
  "title": "n8n / Queue Mode",
  "tags": [
    "n8n"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "editable": true,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "label": "Data source",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "current": {
          "text": "Prometheus",
          "value": "prometheus"
        },
        "hide": 0
      },
      {
        "name": "job",
        "label": "Job",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${datasource}"
        },
        "query": "label_values(up, job)",
        "current": {
          "text": "n8n",
          "value": "n8n"
        },
        "refresh": 1,
        "includeAll": false,
        "multi": false,
        "sort": 1,
        "hide": 0
      },
      {
        "name": "instance",
        "label": "Instance",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "${datasource}"
        },
        "query": "label_values(up{job=\"$job\"}, instance)",
        "current": {
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        },
        "refresh": 2,
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true,
        "sort": 1,
        "hide": 0
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Queue mode: read this first",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "description": "Why this dashboard is empty on most first runs, and which flags it depends on.",
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Queue depth gauges are collected on the **main** instance only; workers never expose them. Scrape both roles: main for queue depth, every worker for process health. Zeros here usually mean only a worker is scraped, or the queue flag sits on a worker.\n\nMain needs `N8N_METRICS_INCLUDE_QUEUE_METRICS` and `N8N_METRICS_INCLUDE_MESSAGE_EVENT_BUS_METRICS`; every worker needs `N8N_METRICS` and the event-bus flag. See the README; `scripts/doctor.sh` reports what each target has."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Queue depth (main instance)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 10
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Jobs waiting",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 11
      },
      "description": "Jobs enqueued in Redis that no worker has picked up yet. This is a gauge, so it is read directly with no rate(). Taken as the maximum across scraped targets because every main reports the same shared queue and summing would multiply the depth by the number of mains. Requires N8N_METRICS_INCLUDE_QUEUE_METRICS on the main instance. The gauge is refreshed on the interval set by N8N_METRICS_QUEUE_METRICS_INTERVAL, 20 seconds by default, so it lags reality by up to that interval. The thresholds are starting values, not a rule.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 25
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 100
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "max(n8n_scaling_mode_queue_jobs_waiting{job=\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"})",
          "legendFormat": "waiting",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Jobs active",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 11
      },
      "description": "Jobs currently held by a worker and executing. A gauge, read directly with no rate(). If active sits at the total worker concurrency while waiting keeps climbing, the workers are saturated and more worker capacity is needed. Requires N8N_METRICS_INCLUDE_QUEUE_METRICS on the main instance.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "blue",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "max(n8n_scaling_mode_queue_jobs_active{job=\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"})",
          "legendFormat": "active",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Targets up for job $job",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 11
      },
      "description": "How many scrape targets of this job answered the last scrape, counting mains and workers together. In queue mode this should equal one main plus the number of workers. A number lower than that means a target is down or missing from prometheus/targets/*.yml.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(up{job=\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"})",
          "legendFormat": "targets up",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Targets exposing queue metrics",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 18,
        "y": 11
      },
      "description": "How many scraped targets publish the queue depth gauges. Zero means no main instance is being scraped, or N8N_METRICS_INCLUDE_QUEUE_METRICS is not set on the main. Workers never publish these gauges, so a value of zero with several targets up is the signature of scraping workers only.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "count(n8n_scaling_mode_queue_jobs_waiting{job=\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "targets with queue gauges",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Queue depth over time",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16
      },
      "description": "Waiting and active job counts as reported by the main instance. Both are gauges and are graphed as read, without rate(). Healthy queue mode keeps waiting near zero with active moving up and down as work arrives. Requires N8N_METRICS_INCLUDE_QUEUE_METRICS on the main instance.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 15,
            "showPoints": "auto",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "gradientMode": "none",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "max(n8n_scaling_mode_queue_jobs_waiting{job=\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"})",
          "legendFormat": "waiting"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "max(n8n_scaling_mode_queue_jobs_active{job=\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"})",
          "legendFormat": "active"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Backlog trend",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "description": "The waiting queue together with the rate at which it is changing. A rising line means jobs are arriving faster than the workers finish them, so the workers cannot keep up and the backlog is growing. A backlog change above zero for a sustained period is the point to add workers or reduce the trigger rate. Below zero the queue is draining. Requires N8N_METRICS_INCLUDE_QUEUE_METRICS on the main instance.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 16
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "decimals": 2,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 15,
            "showPoints": "auto",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "gradientMode": "none",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "backlog change"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "unit",
                "value": "ops"
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.axisPlacement",
                "value": "right"
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.fillOpacity",
                "value": 0
              },
              {
                "id": "custom.lineWidth",
                "value": 2
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "max(n8n_scaling_mode_queue_jobs_waiting{job=\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"})",
          "legendFormat": "waiting"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "deriv(max(n8n_scaling_mode_queue_jobs_waiting{job=\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"})[10m:1m])",
          "legendFormat": "backlog change"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Job throughput",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Queue job completion and failure rate",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 25
      },
      "description": "Completed and failed jobs per second, taken from the queue counters on the main instance. These are counters and reset when the main restarts, so they are always read through rate(). The maximum across targets is used rather than the sum, because every main reports the same shared queue. Requires N8N_METRICS_INCLUDE_QUEUE_METRICS on the main instance.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "decimals": 2,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "auto",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "gradientMode": "none",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "failed"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "max(rate(n8n_scaling_mode_queue_jobs_completed{job=\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "completed"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "max(rate(n8n_scaling_mode_queue_jobs_failed{job=\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "failed"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Job lifecycle rate (event bus)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 25
      },
      "description": "Every stage a job passes through, per second, from the event bus counters. Enqueued is emitted by the main when a job is pushed to Redis; dequeued, completed, failed and stalled are emitted by the worker that handled the job, so these series are summed across all targets. Stalled means a worker took a job and then stopped reporting progress, so the queue considered it abandoned and put it back for another worker to pick up; it usually points at a worker that was killed, ran out of memory, or blocked its event loop. Enqueued running above dequeued is the same backlog condition shown above. Requires N8N_METRICS_INCLUDE_MESSAGE_EVENT_BUS_METRICS on the main and on every worker. These counters reset on restart, so they are read through rate().",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ops",
          "decimals": 2,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "linear",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "auto",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "gradientMode": "none",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "failed"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "red"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "stalled"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "orange"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(n8n_queue_job_enqueued_total{job=\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "enqueued"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(n8n_queue_job_dequeued_total{job=\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "dequeued"
        },
        {
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(n8n_queue_job_completed_total{job=\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "completed"
        },
        {
          "refId": "D",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(n8n_queue_job_failed_total{job=\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "failed"
        },
        {
          "refId": "E",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(n8n_queue_job_stalled_total{job=\"$job\", instance=~\"$instance\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "stalled"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Worker health",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 33
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Targets: one row per instance",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 34
      },
      "description": "Every scrape target of this job side by side, so one sick worker stands out against the others. Up is the scrape result. Leader is n8n_instance_role_leader, which only main instances publish: a row with an empty Leader column is a worker, a row with 1 is the leader main. CPU is cores used, where 1 means one full core. Event loop lag p99 above roughly 100 ms means that instance is blocking on synchronous work and will be slow to accept or finish jobs. CPU, memory and lag come from N8N_METRICS_INCLUDE_DEFAULT_METRICS, which is on by default.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto",
            "cellOptions": {
              "type": "auto"
            },
            "filterable": true
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Up"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "custom.cellOptions",
                "value": {
                  "type": "color-background"
                }
              },
              {
                "id": "mappings",
                "value": [
                  {
                    "type": "value",
                    "options": {
                      "0": {
                        "text": "down",
                        "color": "red",
                        "index": 0
                      },
                      "1": {
                        "text": "up",
                        "color": "green",
                        "index": 1
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "Leader"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "mappings",
                "value": [
                  {
                    "type": "value",
                    "options": {
                      "0": {
                        "text": "main (follower)",
                        "index": 0
                      },
                      "1": {
